# write_execute -- a declaration the grammar itself refuses.
#
# The permission grammar holds `r`, `rw`, and `rx`, and nothing else. A
# document asking for `rwx` is refused at its own line with `BadPermission`,
# so W xor X is a property of what a declaration CAN SAY rather than a check
# run afterward on what it happened to say.

system write_execute

domain worker

region code 4096

grant code worker rwx
